Subject: wpewebkit: depend on libwpe, not on wpebackend-fdo

WPE WebKit links libwpe; the *backend* is a shared object dlopen'd at runtime
and selected by WPE_BACKEND. Buildroot nonetheless makes wpebackend-fdo a hard
dependency, and fdo is built on Wayland -- it needs wayland, libepoxy and
EGL_WL_bind_wayland_display.

That makes WPE unbuildable on a system whose EGL has no Wayland support at all.
Imagination's DDK for PowerVR SGX 5-series is such a system: its WSEGL layer
offers X11/DRI, LinuxFB, Front, Blit and Flip, and predates Wayland entirely.
The gate is in the packaging rather than in WPE itself -- MiniBrowser and the
API tests are what normally want a concrete backend, and Buildroot already
configures both OFF.

The replacement is libwpe rather than nothing. Buildroot never lists libwpe as
a wpewebkit dependency at all: WPEWEBKIT_DEPENDENCIES reaches it only through
wpebackend-fdo, whose own DEPENDENCIES include it, and BR2_PACKAGE_LIBWPE is
set only because wpebackend-fdo's Config.in selects it. Confirmed on a live
tree, where the config reads

  # BR2_PACKAGE_LIBWPE is not set
  BR2_PACKAGE_WPEBACKEND_FDO=y

while libwpe is built anyway. Deleting the fdo dependency without putting libwpe
in its place therefore removes WebKit's only ordering guarantee on a library it
genuinely links (wpe-webkit-2.0.pc carries "Requires: ... wpe-1.0").

Removing fdo from WPEWEBKIT_DEPENDENCIES is also not enough on its own, because
Config.in SELECTS it, and kconfig honours a select regardless of the .mk. So
wayland, wayland-protocols and a Wayland backend that cannot work on this EGL
were all built and installed into the rootfs anyway. The selects have to go too.

wayland-protocols goes with them: it is pulled in only for fdo.

A build that does want the fdo backend still gets it by selecting it directly.

Deliberately left alone: the menuconfig `comment` block above still lists
!BR2_PACKAGE_HAS_LIBEGL_WAYLAND among the reasons wpewebkit is unavailable, so
that hint is now wrong. It is a display string in a UI this tree never opens --
build.sh goes straight to defconfig -- and touching it would add another hunk
for a Buildroot bump to break, which is a worse trade than an inaccurate hint.

Note that dropping the selects stops fdo and wayland being BUILT, but Buildroot
never uninstalls a deselected package's files, so libWPEBackend-fdo and the
libwayland-* already in target/ survive until a clean build. They are inert --
libWPEBackend-default.so.1 points at the PowerVR backend -- just dead weight.

--- a/package/wpewebkit/wpewebkit.mk	2026-08-28 19:13:38
+++ b/package/wpewebkit/wpewebkit.mk	2026-08-28 19:13:38
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 WPEWEBKIT_CPE_ID_PRODUCT = wpe_webkit
 WPEWEBKIT_DEPENDENCIES = host-gperf host-python3 host-ruby host-unifdef \
 	harfbuzz cairo icu jpeg libepoxy libgcrypt libgles libsoup3 libtasn1 \
-	libpng libxslt wayland-protocols webp wpebackend-fdo
+	libpng libxslt libwpe webp
 
 WPEWEBKIT_CMAKE_BACKEND = ninja
 
--- a/package/wpewebkit/Config.in	2026-08-28 19:13:38
+++ b/package/wpewebkit/Config.in	2026-08-28 19:13:38
@@ -41,7 +41,6 @@
 	depends on BR2_USE_WCHAR # icu, libsoup3
 	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HAS_LIBGLES # libepoxy
 	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HAS_LIBEGL # libepoxy
-	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HAS_LIBEGL_WAYLAND # wpebackend-fdo
 	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_WPEWEBKIT_ARCH_SUPPORTS
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_CAIRO
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_CAIRO_PNG
@@ -53,12 +52,10 @@
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBPNG
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBSOUP3
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBTASN1
+	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBWPE
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBXSLT
-	select BR2_PACKAGE_WAYLAND
-	select BR2_PACKAGE_WAYLAND_PROTOCOLS
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_WEBP
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_WEBP_DEMUX
-	select BR2_PACKAGE_WPEBACKEND_FDO
 	help
 	  WPE (Web Platform for Embedded) port of the WebKit engine,
 	  to allow embedders to create simple and performant systems
